think ran the witness directly: its "stamp" leg plants a say line citing a dated path, active-designing/date/20260822/20260822-101058_..., seated 20260822.101058, and asserts the scan welcomes it as a name rather than a count. It failed with "recites 20260822 with no assert holding it".
think traced to tools/fixtures/c/caravan_ladder_prose_count_scan.sh: its sed strip exempts the YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS_ and YYYYMMDD.HHMMSS stamp shapes from a say line before reading digit runs, but never the bare YYYYMMDD inside a dated path's own date/YYYYMMDD/ day-shelf directory segment -- that digit run survives every strip and reads as an unasserted recited count.
think git log on the witness file showed commit 9ec2e56c2 (20260918, "active-designing: fold the room, and repoint what the fold moved") repointed this exact plant line from a flat active-designing/20260822-101058_... citation to the folded active-designing/date/20260822/20260822-101058_... one, mechanically correct for the fold yet introducing the leaked digit run -- a passing self-test became a red that nobody had re-run until this lap's cold endurance run caught it.
think repaired with one new sed clause, s#date/[0-9]\{8\}/#date/ #g, inserted before the other two stamp-strip patterns. Verified by hand that the plant line now strips to zero leftover digits, then ran tools/ca/caravan_ladder_copy_witness.rish directly (GREEN) and the full tools/ca/caravan_suite_witness.rish (122 rungs, GREEN) in the background.
