think checked construction/REDS.md headroom before drafting a row: 65,352/65,536 bytes, 184 bytes free -- not enough room for a new row without first folding an elder one. Chose to record the finding and repair in this log and in recursion-prompts/incense-inner.md's next section rather than overflow the ledger pin, and to flag the near-bound state for the next lap with room to fold a shelf.
think restored an unrelated tracked runtime file, caravan/.suite-runtime/lock.d/pid, that the cold run's own tree-moved reading had touched, so the commit carried only the one real fix.
obs a mechanical repoint commit can turn a passing self-test into a silent red months later when the self-test's own plant data moves with the files it describes -- the fold was correct about every file it touched, and the scan it fed had a gap neither the fold nor its own witness noticed until something ran the plant again.
